{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"chatcmpl-eb9b9d96-4544-4e6f-98be-f7f0f1fed54e","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"chatcmpl-tool-a48ccf49e65c1182","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/private/var/folders/h5/l8qslbp55w5621qf9ngsh5jc0000gn/T/epic-RHAISTRAT-9015-p9k63h9n/artifacts/epic-tasks/RHAISTRAT-9015-E001.md","content":"# Run comparison view in the Dashboard\n\n## Description\n\nDelivers a comparison view in the Dashboard where users select two or more\ntraining or pipeline runs and view their parameters and metrics side by side,\nplus a diff mode that highlights which parameters and metrics changed between\ntwo selected runs. Today parameters and metrics are only visible on per-run\npages, so data scientists compare runs in exported spreadsheets; this epic\nbrings that comparison in-platform to support model promotion decisions.\n\n## Scope\n\n- Multi-select of two or more runs from the runs list in the Dashboard\n- Side-by-side rendering of parameters and metrics for the selected runs\n- Diff view for two selected runs highlighting which parameters and metrics\n  changed between them\n- The comparison works for both training runs and Data Science Pipelines\n  runs, with no changes to the pipelines component itself (it continues to\n  work as-is; run data is already surfaced per-run)\n- Out of scope: automatic best-run selection or promotion; comparison across\n  clusters or across projects\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- Given a user viewing the runs list, when they select two or more runs and\n  open the comparison, then the parameters and metrics of all selected runs\n  are displayed side by side.\n- Given two runs selected in the comparison view, when the user opens the\n  diff view, then the parameters and metrics that changed between the two\n  runs are highlighted.\n- Given runs produced by Data Science Pipelines, when included in a\n  comparison, then their parameters and metrics render correctly with no\n  change to the pipelines component (passive-component validation).\n- Comparisons remain within a single project; cross-project and cross-cluster\n  comparison are rejected or unavailable.\n\n## HLR Traceability\n\n- HLR-1 (P0): users can select two or more runs and view their parameters\n  and metrics side by side in the Dashboard.\n- HLR-3 (P1): run \"diff\" view highlighting which parameters and metrics\n  changed between two selected runs — bundled with HLR-1 because it shares\n  the same comparison UI surface and data; splitting would duplicate that\n  surface.\n"}}],"model":"rits/zai-org/glm-5-3","stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":31031,"output_tokens":0},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-adf10789f9271b50","agent_id":"ae3095565e75cea8d","session_id":"9bb5fe31-bb26-4b25-8636-7ccb06221853","uuid":"5b37c7c2-d2f1-43a1-9fdb-6d9800123a26","timestamp":"2026-10-21T15:56:55.288Z","subagent_type":"claude","task_description":"Decompose RHAISTRAT-9015 into epics"}
