ing API\n53\t  surface without custom tooling.\n54\t- Given model versions registered before this change, when queried, then they\n55\t  continue to function (no migration breakage; absence of lineage on legacy\n56\t  versions is handled gracefully).\n57\t\n58\t## HLR Traceability\n59\t\n60\t- HLR-2 (P1): registered model versions link back to the run that produced\n61\t  them (metadata portion of the requirement).\n62\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-8d4578c2638374ef","agent_id":"a323b47d8b99a5376","session_id":"9bb5fe31-bb26-4b25-8636-7ccb06221853","uuid":"a17c532e-f457-48ca-89d5-69a419fbae71","timestamp":"2026-10-21T15:59:23.577Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-aeb42a69d8d86769","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"claude","task_description":"Review RHAISTRAT-9015 decomposition"}
