{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-8f0b5f236a233fd4","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t---\n2\tstrat_id: RHAISTRAT-9015\n3\tscore: 14\n4\tpass: true\n5\trecommendation: accept\n6\tissues:\n7\t- severity: minor\n8\t  criterion: HLR Coverage\n9\t  description: E001 bundles HLR-3 (P1 diff view) with HLR-1 (P0); bundling is justified\n10\t    by shared UI surface but the diff view is a distinct capability — acceptable as-is,\n11\t    revisit only if independent deferral becomes a planning need\n12\t- severity: minor\n13\t  criterion: AI Implementability Scoring\n14\t  description: 'human_process_gates asymmetry: E001 scores 0 (hedging on possible\n15\t    undeclared UX review) while E002 scores 1 with the equivalent no-gates-declared\n16\t    situation; each rationale supports its own value but the treatment is inconsistent'\n17\terror: null\n18\t---\n19\t# Decomposition Review — RHAISTRAT-9015\n20\t\n21\t## Review Summary\n22\t\n23\tScore: 14/14 — pass\n24\tRecommendation: accept\n25\t\n26\tReviewed against the strategy (RHAISTRAT-9015, Refinement Done, Major), the\n27\tdecomposition summary, 4 epic files, and 4 AI signal rationale files. No\n28\tconditional branch files exist (none required — no open questions or external\n29\tdependencies). Architecture context verified: dashboard.md, model-registry.md,\n30\tand data-science-pipelines.md all present under rhoai-3.0; owning-team fields\n31\t(RHOAI Dashboard, Model Registry) match the epic assignments. Triage is null\n32\t(full decomposition), so the 4-epic output is expected and not penalized.\n33\t\n34\t## Criterion Details\n35\t\n36\t### 1. HLR Coverage (2/2)\n37\tAll four HLRs map to at least one epic: HLR-1 (P0) → E001; HLR-2 (P1) → E002 +\n38\tE003 (correctly split by component); HLR-3 (P1) → E001; HLR-4 (P2) → E004.\n39\tTraceability matrix is present in the summary and mirrored in each epic's HLR\n40\tTraceability section. Priority inheritance is sound: E001 (P0) blocks only\n41\tlower-or-equal priority work (E003 P1, E004 P1); E004's P1 (vs HLR-4's P2)\n42\tcorrectly applies the docs-authoring exception (strategy priority Major → P1).\n43\tMinor (no score impact): E001 bundles HLR-1 (P0) with HLR-3 (P1) — the diff\n44\tview is a distinct user-facing capability, but the bundling is explicitly\n45\tjustified by shared UI surface and data plumbing (same component, team, and\n46\tview; splitting would revisit the same surface), which is a defensible\n47\tStep-4 coupling call rather than priority collapse of independently\n48\tdeferrable work.\n49\t\n50\t### 2. DAG Coherence (2/2)\n51\tNo cycles. Every diagram edge has a matching frontmatter dependency and vice\n52\tversa: E003 depends on [E001, E002]; E004 depends on [E001, E002, E003]; E001\n53\tand E002 are roots. Arrows are drawn dependency → dependent per convention.\n54\tEdges are justified: E001→E003 (surface → consumer, rule 13), E002→E003\n55\t(lineage artifact consumer, rule 13), and the three edges into E004 are valid\n56\trule 11 docs-authoring edges. E001 ∥ E002 correctly preserve parallelism\n57\t(separate repos, no shared artifact). Critical path length 3 fits the\n58\tstrategy size (S/M standard: 3-4). No konflux-onboarding epics exist, so\n59\trules 7/8/10 parallelism constraints are not applicable. No branch files, so\n60\tbranch/gated_by checks are not applicable. No uncaptured data dependencies:\n61\tE003's scope explicitly names its two upstream capabilities and both are DAG\n62\tedges.\n63\t\n64\t### 3. Epic Boundaries (2/2)\n65\tEach epic is a single component/team tuple: E001/E003 (Dashboard, RHOAI\n66\tDashboard), E002 (Model Registry, Model Registry), E004 (Documentation, RHOAI\n67\tDocumentation). HLR-2 is correctly split along the component boundary\n68\t(metadata vs UI entry point) rather than bundled. No scope duplication: E003\n69\tadds an entry point to the comparison view E001 builds without rebuilding it;\n70\tE002 produces the lineage E003 consumes. Code implementation (E001-E003) is\n71\tcleanly separated from content authoring (E004). Each epic is plausibly\n72\tsingle-sprint sized.\n73\t\n74\t### 4. Type Correctness (2/2)\n75\tAll four epics are Implementation; each produces a concrete artifact (UI\n76\tview, lineage metadata, UI entry point, documentation). No Investigation\n77\tepics — justified: the strategy states \"Open Questions: None\" and the summary\n78\texplains why remaining unknowns (bulk-fetch mechanics, lineage storage) are\n79\timplementation details that do not change epic structure. No gated_by or\n80\tgate_failure_impact fields are set anywhere, and none are needed (no\n81\tInvestigation dependencies). E004 correctly carries\n82\timplementation_type: docs-authoring.\n83\t\n84\t### 5. AI Implementability Scoring (2/2)\n85\tAll epics are Implementation type and carry ai_signals (the 9-signal rubric);\n86\tno epic mixes in investigation_signals. Signal values are consistent with the\n87\tstrategy content: e.g., E001/E003 external_dependency 1 (all work in the\n88\tDashboard repo) vs E002 external_dependency 0 (model-registry is\n89\tupstream-derived, contribution possible — neutral), E004 human_process_gates\n90\t-1 (docs content process plus mandatory technical review), E004 repo_access 0\n91\t(docs tooling access unconfirmed). Rationale files exist for all four epics\n92\tand match the frontmatter values. Minor (no score impact): the\n93\thuman_process_gates asymmetry between E001 (0, hedged on possible undeclared\n94\tUX review for a new UI surface) and E002 (1, \"no human approval steps\n95\tdeclared\") is arguable, but each rationale supports its own value and the\n96\tdifference is defensible (new user-facing surface vs metadata-only change).\n97\t\n98\t### 6. Acceptance Criteria Quality (2/2)\n99\tEvery epic has testable acceptance criteria derived from the strategy. E001's\n100\tACs cover multi-select side-by-side rendering, the diff view, passive\n101\tvalidation against Data Science Pipelines runs, and enforcement of the\n102\tstrategy's out-of-scope boundary (no cross-project/cross-cluster comparison).\n103\tE002 includes a backward-compatibility AC for pre-existing model versions.\n104\tE003 covers both the happy path and graceful handling of versions without\n105\tlineage. E004 (docs-authoring) includes the rule-mandated technical-review\n106\tAC. No replacement epics (no rollback/feature-flag AC required) and no\n107\tkonflux-chain epics (no build pipeline AC required). No epic body references\n108\tsibling epics by draft ID — E003 refers to \"other work in this strategy\"\n109\twithout naming E001/E002.\n110\t\n111\t### 7. Completeness (2/2)\n112\tThe combined epic set covers the full strategy scope: runs-list multi-select\n113\tand side-by-side view (E001), diff view (E001), run lineage on model versions\n114\t(E002), registry-initiated comparison (E003), and documentation of both entry\n115\tpaths (E004). The strategy's out-of-scope items are explicitly carried into\n116\tE001's scope. Data Science Pipelines is handled as a passive component with\n117\tan explicit validation AC on E001 — no HLR requires a pipelines change, and\n118\tthe summary flags the residual risk if a pipelines-side API change turns out\n119\tto be needed. Strategy-level context is carried forward: the\n120\tspreadheets-to-platform problem statement appears in E001's description, the\n121\ttwo-council source overlap is recorded in the summary's health warnings, and\n122\tteam-inference caveats are documented. Documentation support is required\n123\t(HLR-4) and E004 exists, satisfying Rule 11.\n124\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-bbeda89e2c61a8fc","agent_id":"a854d415f71625cf9","session_id":"9bb5fe31-bb26-4b25-8636-7ccb06221853","uuid":"cf221128-adec-4cdc-8408-009a2408315e","timestamp":"2026-10-21T16:02:28.257Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-8f0b5f236a233fd4","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}